Ubuntu Touch for Samsung Tab S9 (gts9uwifi) - flashable update package

This zip reflashes the boot images and writes a new rootfs onto the existing
system dynamic partition. It carries NO Samsung firmware, so the device must
already run a gts9uwifi Ubuntu Touch build.


First install (once, builds super locally)

The Samsung firmware partitions (vendor, odm, product, ...) are not
redistributable, so super is assembled on your machine:

  1. download the firmware bits:
       https://download.azka.li/ubuntu-touch-kalama-firmware-v.tar.xz
     (super minus system: vendor.img, odm.img, product.img, system_ext.img,
      system_dlkm.img, vendor_dlkm.img)
  2. ./build.sh
  3. extract the tar next to out/, then:
       PARTS=<extracted-dir> OUT=out/super.img scripts/super.sh
  4. flash boot/init_boot/vendor_boot/vbmeta and super in TWRP (see below),
     using out/*.img and out/super.img


Updating (this zip)

Prereq: the device already booted a gts9uwifi Ubuntu Touch build once.

  1. boot TWRP (adb reboot recovery, or vol-up + power)
  2. mount /data in TWRP (Mount -> Data); there is no free space elsewhere
  3. adb push ubuntu-touch-gts9uwifi-update.zip /data/
  4. Install -> /data -> ubuntu-touch-gts9uwifi-update.zip
  5. adb shell twrp reboot system

The updater flashes boot/init_boot/vendor_boot/vbmeta and dd's the rootfs
onto /dev/block/mapper/system. It bundles a static zstd, so recovery needs
nothing extra.


Notes

- Do not "reboot system" from the TWRP menu; it loops back to recovery. Use
  adb shell twrp reboot system.
- Build this zip from a finished ./build.sh with scripts/make-flashable.sh.
